  "comment": "WatchDocMessages frames (crates/doc/src/transcript_delta.rs): each case applies its frames in order to an empty transcript. `expect` is the transcript after the last frame, as each entry's id, role and the text of its text and reasoning parts; `desyncAt` is the index of the frame that must be refused (the client then resubscribes for a reset). Runners: crates/doc/tests/desktop_transcript_vectors.rs (apply_transcript_frame) and apps/nano/src/parity.zig (Transcript.apply).",
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "a reset, an upsert after its anchor, streamed text",
      "frames": [
        {
          "reset": [
            {
              "id": "u1",
              "role": "user",
              "parts": [
                {
                  "kind": "text",
                  "id": "p1",
                  "text": "Add rate limiting"
                }
              ],
              "createdAt": 1,
              "deviceId": "dev-a"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "upsert": [
            {
              "after": "u1",
              "entry": {
                "id": "a1",
                "role": "assistant",
                "parts": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "id": "t1",
                    "text": "Hel"
                  }
                ],
                "createdAt": 1,
                "deviceId": "dev-a",
                "status": "streaming"
              }
            }
          ],
          "append": [],
          "remove": [],
          "count": 2
        },
        {
          "upsert": [],
          "append": [
            {
              "entry": "a1",
              "part": "t1",
              "text": "lo",
              "len": 5
            }
          ],
          "remove": [],
          "count": 2
        }
      ],
      "expect": [
        {
          "id": "u1",
          "role": "user",
          "texts": [
            "Add rate limiting"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "a1",
          "role": "assistant",
          "texts": [
            "Hello"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
